{
  "dom_id": "step-44287",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Expressing Division Problems as Mixed Numbers",
  "problem": "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $(-5) \\div (-3).$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we are dividing a negative number $({\\color{red}-5})$ by another negative number $({\\color{red}-3}).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152110/assets/cce63c47aea469b99cccad529462e33e193ff094efb7d3535cf8ca095d8c23a9.svg)\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 3 = 1 \\,\\textrm{R}\\, 2 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue} 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
